Constant stimulation is the enemy of deep creativity. When every spare second is filled with notifications and feeds, the mind loses the quiet friction required to spark original ideas.

Embracing solitude allows the subconscious to wander, making unexpected connections between distant memories and observations. True innovation often arrives in the quiet space between thoughts.